  "results": "Across 45 cells (20 seeds each, c=[2] primary), the mean paired gap = -0.000 ACC (SD of cell means 0.007). Gap by ratio: r=0.5: -0.001, r=1.0: 0.003, r=1.5: -0.002, r=2.0: -0.001, r=3.0: 0.000. The strongest exploration advantage occurs at c=2, d=5, n=200, ratio=1.0 (gap=0.017, dz=0.31); the smallest gap occurs at c=2, d=10, n=200, ratio=2.0 (gap=-0.019, dz=-0.48). In the OLS, ratio coef=-0.0002 (p=0.841), d coef=-0.0003 (p=0.481), n coef=0.00000 (p=0.331).",
  "conclusion": "On the partial c=2 synthetic-GMM grid available at hand-off, the paired gap between P2_Full and P2_NoExploration is statistically indistinguishable from zero: mean gap = -0.000 ACC, OLS R^2 = 0.002, and no factor (ratio, d, n, nor the ratio:d / ratio:n interactions) reaches p<0.05. The pre-registered expectation that the exploration reward grows under heavier overlap (smaller ratio) is NOT supported by this slice (ratio coef=-0.0002, p=0.841). Cell-level gaps scatter symmetrically around zero (max +0.017, min -0.019 ACC), consistent with sampling noise. This unit is exploratory/underpowered: c=3 and d=20 cells are still being appended in the background; the null verdict may revise once the full grid lands, but no directional exploration advantage is visible so far.",
  "support": "not supported",
  "annotations": [
    "supportive",
    "exploratory",
    "underpowered: c=3 and d=20 arms not run; inference on c=2, d in {2,5,10}",
    "partial grid: 900/3200 rows, c=2 subset, c=3 deferred, underpowered",
    "20 seeds",
    "synthetic control (no real benchmark)"
  ],
